  "findings": [
    "All six samples complete developer/tester/reviewer checks, six independent tests, the intended clamp.py merge, worktree cleanup and unchanged completed work after restart.",
    "Original median 4.685 seconds; ACP median 10.597 seconds. This is an observed wall-time regression, not acceleration.",
    "Original launches three useful turns and two idle turns; ACP launches exactly three useful turns. Checks and workflow mutations move from the deterministic agent fixture to the daemon."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three samples per version on one host, no statistical speed guarantee.",
    "Both continuously running public daemon CLIs use a 0.2-second interval; no idle conversation or run history is seeded. Setup, final independent checks and restart verification are outside the timing.",
    "Fixtures implement equivalent outcomes through different native versus ACP contracts. Schemas and dependencies necessarily differ; this is an architecture comparison, not a single-change experiment.",
    "Original package code is unmodified. Its private canon overrides only auto_update.mode=disabled to prevent update checking. Original gates still run.",
    "The original cline executable is a private deterministic wrapper, not Cline or a provider. No model, login, billed-token or quality claim.",
    "Original checks restart through public daemon reconcile logs; ACP checks core serve once and exact durable run/result/command equality.",
    "Earlier exploratory original samples and profiling runs are excluded."
  ]
